#
# The continuing goal, retired by a week that went well.
#
# The cluster's standing goal is a MAINTENANCE target: the decision record is current at
# every state of the interval, and the interval is the life of the cluster. Week 12 ran,
# the review was held, minuted and published, and somebody judged the standing goal against
# that week — reasonably, and wrongly. The evaluation says logic:Satisfied, which is true
# so far, and logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, which is the claim that the judgment is now
# CONCLUSIVE.
#
# Nothing here is missing. The evaluation binds all four factored axes plus its criterion
# and its time; the goal carries a well-formed logic:GoalExpression; the expression names
# its bound situation type. Every presence law the kernel and the shape surface author
# passes. The defect is the JOIN between the goal's compositional kind and the
# conclusiveness the evaluation claims: a maintenance target has no state at which "held
# every time so far" becomes "will hold", so its window never closes and the conclusive
# judgment is unreachable.
#
# What it costs in the world: (logic:Satisfied, logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted) is EXACTLY
# the pair that generates the conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edge. Generate one here and the
# cluster reads as finished — the recurrence keeps issuing occurrences against a goal the
# record says was closed in March, and the first reviewer who notices concludes the
# schedule is stale rather than the closure being false. A standing commitment becomes a
# cron job nobody can justify, and the evidence that it was ever a commitment is gone.
#
# It is deliberately NOT the windowed case. A maintenance target indexed to a closing
# interval is authored as a logic:DeadlineWindowGoal whose operand carries the maintenance
# sub-expression, so the goal's own logic:hasGoalCondition names the windowed kind and the
# law's guard never reaches it: once that window closes the judgment may conclude, exactly
# as logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted's own definition says. What may never conclude satisfied
# is the unbounded one below.
#
# Nor is it the FAILURE case. A maintenance target that breaks reaches
# logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted with logic:Violated, and that must stay expressible — the
# law forbids the satisfied-and-concluded pair alone.
#
# MUST trip logic:MaintenanceGoalNeverConclusivelySatisfiedConstraint.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

# The continuing goal, and the maintenance reading carried as a VALUE on its compositional
# expression rather than as a type — logic:MaintenanceGoal is a logic:GoalExpressionKind
# individual, and using it as a class would fork the one canonical goal concept into a
# subclass per temporal shape.
ex:decisionsStayReviewed a gmeow:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "Architectural decisions stay reviewed"@en ;
    logic:hasGoalCondition ex:decisionsStayReviewedCondition .

ex:decisionsStayReviewedCondition a logic:GoalExpression ;
    rdfs:label "Maintenance: the decision record is current at every state of the interval"@en ;
    logic:goalExpressionKind logic:MaintenanceGoal ;
    logic:boundSituationType ex:decisionRecordCurrent .

ex:decisionRecordCurrent a logic:Situation ;
    rdfs:label "Every landed decision has been reviewed against the current architecture"@en .

# The judgment that closes it. Complete on every axis, and conclusive about something no
# occurrence can conclude.
ex:maintenanceGoalClosedByWeek12 a logic:GoalEvaluation ;
    rdfs:label "The cluster's maintenance goal, judged against one successful week and marked concluded"@en ;
    logic:evaluatesGoal ex:decisionsStayReviewed ;
    logic:evaluatedAgainst ex:decisionRecordCurrent ;
    logic:evaluationCriterion ex:adrQualityRubric ;
    logic:evaluationTime "2026-03-19T15:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    logic:satisfactionStatus logic:Satisfied ;
    logic:feasibilityStatus logic:Feasible ;
    logic:lifecycleStatus logic:LifecycleActive ;
    logic:goalEvaluationStatus logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted .

ex:adrQualityRubric a gmeow:Rubric ;
    rdfs:label "ADR quality rubric"@en .
